{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1461866-story-uses-for-the-elysians","id":1461866,"title":"Story-Uses for the Elysians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-28T14:22:13-07:00","id":1461866,"title":"Story-Uses for the Elysians","content":"They're haughty. They're entitled. They think they're better than you and, you know what?, they might be right. Look at the way they compose themselves, the way they command all attention whenever they walk into a room. Look at how they've mastered death and the small god incubating inside them. Look at how the Mandate of Heaven flows effortlessly into their perfectly manicured fingers, so smooth, so tapered, so <i>en vogue</i> it makes you want to crash a semi truck into the Louvre. They may as well be the Dallas of the dearly undeparted the way they flaunt and preen and coif with the best ghost-goo money can buy.<br /> <br /> All that, and I really have no idea how to actually use them. I can see easily a number of ways in which Bonepickers, Gatekeepers, and Thanatologists might serve as antagonists to a Sin-Eater krewe, but the Elysians. . . frankly I'm at a loss. They just stand there and sneer at you for wearing a jacket that was all the rage in Seattle maybe five hours ago, but not now, honey, oh <i>bless your heart</i>. But what do they want? How might they stand in the way of necrojustice? Among the living, the rich and powerful rig the system in their favor from top to bottom like it's second nature, but the Bound don't really have a societal overstructure to cheat in the same way. You could just let them be and let them have their little Greek Hero LARP f\u00eate and at most you could only accuse them of not helping out. But there's got to be more than that.<br /> <br /> So anyway, how have you used Elysians in your Geist games? What are some interesting story hooks that involve those Bound who think death is for the little people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T16:47:50-07:00","id":1461888,"title":"","content":"Imagine your favorite flavor of bigot and discriminatory jackass.<br /> <br /> Give them the ability to craft afterlives and mystically control people.<br /> <br /> I ran a one shot once with an Elysian krewe heading a chapter of the Proud Boys who were trying to subvert a Dominion for their followers and making deals with Reapers to facilitate the transport of the people they hate to that Dominion. The player krewe lived up to their Furious Archetype in response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T21:53:44-07:00","id":1461913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1461866-story-uses-for-the-elysians?p=1461888#post1461888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine your favorite flavor of bigot and discriminatory jackass.<br /> <br /> Give them the ability to craft afterlives and mystically control people.<br /> <br /> I ran a one shot once with an Elysian krewe heading a chapter of the Proud Boys who were trying to subvert a Dominion for their followers and making deals with Reapers to facilitate the transport of the people they hate to that Dominion. The player krewe lived up to their Furious Archetype in response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh geez, that's pretty grim. I hadn't considered using them to model bigots, but I can see how that slots in to the Archetype pretty neatly. On a more abstracted level, I guess you could say that they see something they want and just take it, damn everyone else.<br /> <br /> (Also note to self: Homebrew Elysian Ceremony that gives the Bound limited control over who their death gets shunted onto.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T17:21:40-07:00","id":1462047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1461866-story-uses-for-the-elysians?p=1461913#post1461913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh geez, that's pretty grim. I hadn't considered using them to model bigots, but I can see how that slots in to the Archetype pretty neatly. On a more abstracted level, I guess you could say that they see something they want and just take it, damn everyone else.<br /> <br /> (Also note to self: Homebrew Elysian Ceremony that gives the Bound limited control over who their death gets shunted onto.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. THe core of the Elysians is that they believe they deserve more and better than everyone else, and they have the ability to <i>act</i> on that. When the book says that the Bound have the power to change the world, <i>they don't neccesarily mean for the better</i>.<br /> <br /> Once you know <i>who</i> they think they deserve more than, the plots bubble up from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}